{"name":"Tenné","hex":"#cd5700","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tenné","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A rarely-used tincture of orange or bright brown."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Orange or bright brown."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tenn%C3%A9"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tenné","blocks":[{"text":"In heraldry, tenné is a \"stain\", or non-standard tincture, of orange, light brown or orange-tawny colour."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tenn%C3%A9","wikidata":"Q218169"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Complete_Guide_to_Heraldry_Fig036.png/500px-Complete_Guide_to_Heraldry_Fig036.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Complete_Guide_to_Heraldry_Fig036.png/500px-Complete_Guide_to_Heraldry_Fig036.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Fig. 36 from Fox-Davies, Complete Guide to Heraldry (1909): Extended hatching scheme used in continental heraldry. a, Tenné; b, blood-red (Sanguine); c, earth-brown (Brunâtre); d, Iron; e, water-colour or Bleu céleste; f, flesh-colour or Carnation; g, ashen-grey or Cendrée; h, orange; and i, colour of nature (proper).","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AComplete_Guide_to_Heraldry_Fig036.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Burgos-Bandera.jpg/120px-Burgos-Bandera.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Burgos-Bandera.jpg/250px-Burgos-Bandera.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Burgos-Bandera.jpg/120px-Burgos-Bandera.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki